# repo-guard allowlist. Format: path-glob [| rule [| text]]
# text is a substring of the match or sha256:<hex prefix> (see --show-digest).
# Never put real private values here; use sha256: entries instead.

# Exemptions are per value, never per directory: a blanket rule once hid a real
# lab address in a test file. New fixtures should prefer 192.0.2.0/24.
# Go test fixtures: fake gateways, adapters and parser edge cases.
*_test.go | private-ipv4 | 192.168.1.
*_test.go | private-ipv4 | 192.168.2.0
*_test.go | private-ipv4 | 192.168.001.020
*_test.go | private-ipv4 | 192.000.2.1
*_test.go | private-ipv4 | 10.99.0.
*_test.go | private-ipv4 | 10.21.32.43
*_test.go | private-ipv4 | 10.0.0.1
# Documentation example: fake ZGW bind address.
cmd/fakezgw/README.md | private-ipv4 | 192.168.1.50
docs/CONTRACTS.md | private-ipv4 | 192.168.1.50
docs/DESIGN.md | private-ipv4 | 192.168.1.50
# Addresses quoted from public third-party logs.
docs/enet-protocol-research.md | private-ipv4 | 192.168.16.
# Synthetic VIN in a UI fixture (sequential digits).
internal/ui/view_test.go | vin

# The guard and its tests contain rule patterns and synthetic samples of every rule.
tools/repo-guard.py
tools/test_repo_guard.py

# This file lists only the public example values above.
.repo-guard-allow | private-ipv4
# PEM header literal used to validate the issuer key file format.
internal/ticket/issuer.go | private-key
